WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.501
-Welcome, welcome,
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:04.070
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:05.772
Thank you, guys, so much
for being here.

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:06.873
Let's get to some jokes here.

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:08.007
Last night was

00:00:08.007 --> 00:00:10.176
the National Christmas Tree
Lighting

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:12.545
and, during his speech,
President Biden tried

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:15.548
to thank LL Cool J for hosting.

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:18.918
But I think he was a little
confused about who LL Cool J is.

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:21.254
[ Laughter ]
Watch this.

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:23.589
-A special thanks
to "The Tonight Show's"

00:00:23.589 --> 00:00:25.524
[ Monotone ]
LL Cool J.

00:00:25.524 --> 00:00:27.227
[ Laughter ]
I tell you, what, man.

00:00:27.227 --> 00:00:29.228
He looks like he can still play.

00:00:29.228 --> 00:00:31.630
And I'm not talking
about instruments.

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:32.966
I'm talking about football
or something.

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:34.133
[ Laughter ]
That man is --

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:35.835
Anyway, I tell you what.

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:39.639
[ Laughter and ohs ]

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:40.607
You know, it wouldn't be
the holidays

00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:41.807
without Grandpa saying something

00:00:41.807 --> 00:00:43.977
that makes you go, "Oh, jeez!
Alright. Alright.

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:46.846
[ Laughter and applause ]
Get him outta here."

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:48.548
Biden's staff was going,
"Quick, turn on the tree.

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:49.516
Turn on the tree!"

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:52.118
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:53.920
An aide was like,
"How did that happen?"

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.789
Literally the only thing
on the prompter was...

00:00:57.823 --> 00:01:00.993
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:00.993 --> 00:01:03.963
To be fair, LL Cool J
did play professional football.

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:06.231
In the 1999 movie
"Any Given Sunday."

00:01:06.231 --> 00:01:08.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:08.834 --> 00:01:11.270
It got worse when Biden said,
"Anyway, thanks to --

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:13.405
for whatever you do,
L.L.Bean J."

00:01:13.405 --> 00:01:16.809
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:16.809 --> 00:01:18.711
L.L.Bean J.

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:20.546
Meanwhile, today Biden
was delivering remarks

00:01:20.546 --> 00:01:22.749
on the economy
and he didn't really

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:24.851
sound like himself.
Listen to this.

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:28.087 line:0%
-[ Baritone ]
The CEOs of not only the --

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:29.489 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
the -- the -- the suppliers,

00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:32.658 line:0%
but the CEOs
of UPS and FedEx,

00:01:32.658 --> 00:01:35.128 line:0%
which are on track to deliver
more packages than ever.

00:01:38.464 --> 00:01:41.801
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:43.469
-That was real?
-That's real, yeah.

00:01:43.469 --> 00:01:45.305
There he is, President Groot.

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:49.908
[ Laughter and applause ]
Obama was like --

00:01:49.908 --> 00:01:51.978
[ As Obama ] Sounds like
the job's got you smoking, too.

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:54.013
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:56.315
Overnight, Biden suddenly
turned into Brad Garrett.

00:01:56.315 --> 00:01:57.951
[ As Garrett ]
Raymond, Raymond.

00:01:57.951 --> 00:01:59.151
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.151 --> 00:02:00.286
Even Shaq was like --

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:01.287
[ As Shaq ]
What's up with that voice?

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:05.057
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.057 --> 00:02:07.126
[ Applause ]
Instead of "Hail to the Chief,"

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:09.395
Biden now walks out to this --
[ Yello's "Oh Yeah" plays ]

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:10.796
-♪ Oh yeah ♪

00:02:10.796 --> 00:02:12.831
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]
♪♪

00:02:12.831 --> 00:02:16.869
-[ Mouthing words ]
-♪ Oh yeah ♪

00:02:16.869 --> 00:02:19.005
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:23.876
This is good news -- last night,
just hours before the deadline,

00:02:23.876 --> 00:02:27.213
Congress reached a deal
to avoid a government shutdown.

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:29.882
[ Cheering and applause ]
Yes.

00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:31.650
A government shutdown.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:32.952
You know these are crazy times,

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:34.320
when the government
almost shuts down

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.222
and most Americans are like,
"Meh.

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:38.691
[ Laughter ]
Hey, add it to the pile."

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:40.426
[ Laughter ]
Yeah, the government is now

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:42.695
funded through February 18th.

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:44.998
It's basically Congress'
version of repeatedly clicking

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:46.833
"Remind me tomorrow"
on a software update.

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:48.200
[ Laughter and applause ]
It's like, "No, no, I just want

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:51.370
to check my emails. Not yet, no.
Don't update. Don't."

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.839
Some business news --
Bath &amp; Body Works'

00:02:53.839 --> 00:02:56.608
